ting and empirical forecasts remain unevaluated. No stochastic comparison or method ranking is made.\n\nThe strongest alternative explanation is a shared modeling error between construction and fixtures. Independent posting replay, perturbed inputs and analytic endpoint checks reduce that risk. An in-profile counterexample would overturn this result. The weakest evidence is breadth: these are small deterministic cases, not arbitrary accounting histories.\n\nActual command: `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p04.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04 --execution-inventory data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P04/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json --approved-plan data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P04/approved-plan.json`. Python 3.11.15, Z3 4.16.0, CPU only with GPU devices intentionally hidden. Wall time: 4.406002 seconds. Seeds: N/A, deterministic. Git provenance is unavailable; conformance.json contains content hashes and protection comparisons for 384 files. Current approved plan: `data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P04/approved-plan.json`. Original design: `data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/approved-plan.json`. Current execution inventory: `data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P04/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json`; historical inventory: `data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/phase-entry-inventory.json`. Both references and their hashes are recorded separately. The manifest distinguishes all phase contributions from files changed during this execution.\n\nResiduals: nonlinear inference, continuous probability inference, unbounded integer search, template discovery, general aggregation equivalence, accounting validity, forecast validity and human acceptance remain open. All MC01–MC35/G1–G18 retain wider obligations.\n  312 scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\n  490 scripts/rational_solver_v1.py\n  178 scripts/check_accounting